    "13": {
      "note": "The skill's own statement of the staging contract: a refused gate leaves the worktree fully staged and uncommitted, and because a retry must not inherit that index, each gate run begins with a reset and restages from the working tree, so resetting first recomputes the staged set under the ignore rules in force.\n\nAnchor: \"Staging is **not** undone if the gate refuses.\"",
      "targets": [
